{"name":"Talagbar","status":"ok","title":"Talagbar","pageId":81168,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Talagbar</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"type\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Type</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Mines</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Vaasa\" title=\"Vaasa\">Vaasa</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Cold_Lands\" title=\"Cold Lands\">Cold Lands</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Society</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"races\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Races</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Dwarves\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Dwarves\">Dwarves</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Talagbar</b> was a <a href=\"/wiki/Dwarf\" title=\"Dwarf\">dwarven</a> mine in eastern <a href=\"/wiki/Vaasa\" title=\"Vaasa\">Vaasa</a>. It was considered a \"twin\" of the <a href=\"/wiki/Delhalls\" title=\"Delhalls\">Delhalls</a> in western Vaasa.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p189_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p189-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.81_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.81-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Geography\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Geography</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Geography\">Geography</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Geography\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Talagbar?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Geography\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Talagbar was located in the <a href=\"/wiki/Galena_Mountains\" title=\"Galena Mountains\">Galena Mountains</a> to the east of the road from <a href=\"/wiki/Nigel%27s_Ford\" title=\"Nigel's Ford\">Nigel's Ford</a> to <a href=\"/wiki/Palischuk\" title=\"Palischuk\">Palischuk</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.81_2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-DunMag.177-p.81-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Talagbar?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the 13<sup>th</sup> century <a href=\"/wiki/DR\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"DR\">DR</a>,<sup id=\"cite_ref-RS:Ds_3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-RS:Ds-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Talagbar had long been frozen under the <a href=\"/wiki/Ice_Run\" title=\"Ice Run\">Ice Run</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/Great_Glacier\" title=\"Great Glacier\">Great Glacier</a>, but was believed to be rich with deposits of <a href=\"/wiki/Bloodstone\" title=\"Bloodstone\">bloodstone</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Emerald\" title=\"Emerald\">emerald</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Ruby\" title=\"Ruby\">ruby</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Copper\" title=\"Copper\">copper</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Iron\" title=\"Iron\">iron</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p189_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p189-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup><sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p110_4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p110-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Around <a href=\"/wiki/1372_DR\" title=\"1372 DR\">1372 DR</a>, melting at the edge of the Glacier exposed Talagbar along with its twin, the Delhalls.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS3e-p110_4-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS3e-p110-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> The two mines were said to be so rich in wealth that their discovery changed the culture of Vaasa, making its people more greedy.<sup id=\"cite_ref-RS:Ds_3-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-RS:Ds-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>As of the 15<sup>th</sup> century DR, the mines had been reopened.<sup id=\"cite_ref-FRCS-p189_1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FRCS-p189-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Talagbar?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Talagbar?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-FRCS-p189-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS-p189_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS-p189_1-1\">1.1</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-FRCS-p189_1-2\">1.2</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Bruce_R._Cordell\" title=\"Bruce R. Cordell\">Bruce R. Cordell</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Ed_Greenwood\" title=\"Ed Greenwood\">Ed Greenwood</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Chris_Sims\" title=\"Chris Sims\">Chris Sims</a>&#160;(August 2008). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Forgotten_Realms_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide\">Forgotten Realms Campaign Guide</a></i>. Edited by <a href=\"/wiki/Jennifer_Clarke_Wilkes\" title=\"Jennifer Clarke Wilkes\">Jennifer Clarke Wilkes</a>, <i>et al</i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), p. 189. ISBN&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-7869-4924-3\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-7869-4924-3\">978-0-7869-4924-3</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-DunMag.177-p.81-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.81_2-0\">2.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-DunMag.177-p.81_2-1\">2.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Brian_R._James\" title=\"Brian R. James\">Brian R. James</a>&#160;(April 2010). “Realmslore: Vaasa”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Chris_Youngs\" title=\"Chris Youngs\">Chris Youngs</a>&#160;ed. <a href=\"/wiki/Dungeon_magazine_177\" title=\"Dungeon magazine 177\"><i>Dungeon</i> #177</a> (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>)&#160;(177)., p. 81.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-RS:Ds-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-RS:Ds_3-0\">3.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-RS:Ds_3-1\">3.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Troy_Denning\" title=\"Troy Denning\">Troy Denning</a>&#160;(March 2002). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Realms_of_Shadow\" title=\"Realms of Shadow\">Realms of Shadow</a> (\"Darksword\")</i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>). ISBN&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSource